course: dictionary
lesson: 14049
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mare is a female horse, donkey or zebra, usually an adult one. Its baby is a foal. A male horse is a stallion.
explain: «The mare and her foal walked slowly across the field.» Because a foal is a young horse, mare must mean a female horse here.
explain: Mare has a second meaning in astronomy. «Through the telescope we saw dark patches on the Moon.» Those patches are called maria, the Latin word for sea, because people once thought they were seas.
explain: In everyday English, mare is slang from nightmare. «It was a right mare getting here» means the trip was terrible and annoying. The words around a word, its context, tell you which meaning is right.
fact: Mare means a female horse, donkey or zebra, especially an adult one.
fact: The plural of mare, meaning a dark patch on the Moon, is «maria».
fact: Maria comes from the Latin word for «sea», because people once thought these dark areas were seas.
fact: Mare (UK slang) means a terrible or annoying situation, from «nightmare».
fact: «Having a mare» is UK slang for doing very badly.
exercise: «The mare and her foal grazed by the gate.» What is a foal? | A male horse | *A baby horse | A dark patch on the Moon
exercise: Through a telescope, Maya saw dark patches on the Moon. What is the plural of mare in this meaning? | *Maria | Mayors | Mares | Foals
exercise: «It was a right mare getting here, with three buses and a flat tyre.» What does mare mean here? | A female horse | A calm, lovely journey | A dark patch on the Moon | *A terrible, annoying situation
test: What does the Latin word mare mean? | *Sea | Horse | Moon | Night
test: «She was having a mare with her broken bike.» What does having a mare mean? | Winning a race | Riding a horse | *Doing very badly | Looking at the stars
exam: «The mare galloped across the field with her foal beside her.» What is the mare? | A dark patch on the Moon | *A female horse | A terrible situation | A male horse
